Subject: [hsa-rocr] ppc64le: device-visibility fences, spin hint, image support, vDSO name

Portability fix worth sending upstream (ROCm/rocm-systems, projects/rocr-runtime).

The HSA runtime builds for x86 and, since 7.x, loongarch64, and nothing
else: core/util/utils.h only includes <x86intrin.h> on x86, yet the queue,
doorbell and blit paths call _mm_sfence()/_mm_mfence() unconditionally and
core/util/locks.h spins on _mm_pause(); FlushCacheLines() in utils.h loops
over _mm_clflush().  On ppc64le the build stops at the
first of those with "'_mm_sfence' was not declared in this scope".

What this adds, and why each choice is what it is:

* utils.h gains a __powerpc64__ branch defining the four names (the fences,
  _mm_pause(), and _mm_clflush() as dcbf per line).  Both fences
  are a full `sync`.  Every call site guards a store to memory the GPU reads
  over PCIe -- the doorbell BAR, a device-memory AQL ring, a large-BAR kernarg
  buffer -- and KFD maps those caching-inhibited on POWER.  Power ISA 3.0B
  Book II 4.6.1 restricts lwsync to storage that is "neither Write Through
  Required nor Caching Inhibited", so a release fence (what GCC's own
  <xmmintrin.h> compat header expands _mm_sfence() to) would order nothing
  here; the kernel's writel() on powerpc is `sync; stw` for the same reason.
  _mm_pause() is the kernel's cpu_relax(): lower SMT priority, restore it.
* image/util.h: the "Processor not identified" #error is joined by
  __powerpc64__ next to __loongarch64; the file no longer uses __rdtsc().
* CMakeLists.txt: IMAGE_SUPPORT defaults ON for ppc64le/powerpc64le.  HIP
  refuses a device whose agent lacks the image extension, so OFF is not a
  degraded build, it is no HIP at all.
* os_linux.cpp and amd_hsa_loader.cpp: the two dl_iterate_phdr() callbacks
  skip the vDSO by looking for "vdso.so" in dlpi_name.  The vDSO's soname
  is linux-vdso.so.1 on x86/aarch64 but linux-vdso64.so.1 on ppc64, so the
  filter misses, GetLoadedToolsLib() walks the vDSO's PT_DYNAMIC -- whose
  entries ld.so never relocates in place -- and strcmp()s the link-time
  DT_STRTAB offset (0x2d8) as a pointer.  Every hsa_init() on ppc64le
  segfaulted there.  Match "vdso" instead.

diff -ruN a/runtime/hsa-runtime/CMakeLists.txt b/runtime/hsa-runtime/CMakeLists.txt
